rwp - random word password
==========================
rwp reads a wordlist and prints a passphrase of COUNT random words
joined by SEPARATOR, suitable for use as a password.


Requirements
------------
In order to build rwp you need a C99 compiler (cc, gcc or clang) and a
POSIX system with /dev/urandom.


Installation
------------
Edit config.h to match your local setup (rwp is installed into the
/usr/local namespace by default).

Afterwards enter the following command to build and install rwp (if
necessary as root):

    make clean install


Running rwp
-----------
    usage: rwp [wordlist|-]
           rwp /path/to/wordlist
           rwp

    wordlist    read words from this file (default: WORDLIST in config.h)
    -           read words from standard input


Configuration
-------------
The configuration of rwp is done by creating a custom config.h
and (re)compiling the source code.
